In my current game, I struck a long worm with Magicbane, confusing it.
This led to a message that I hadn't even thought was possible until
now:

"The long worm bites itself. The long worm is killed!"

And no, it wasn't a different long worm being killed on the same turn -
it actually killed itself. A ring of conflict or even a cloak of
displacement can make them attack other creatures, but not themselves.
Or at least, they never did in about 10 minutes of messing around with
both items in wizmode - maybe I'm just not patient enough. Other than a
confused long worm, are there any other circumstances in which a
monster will directly attack and/or kill itself? I couldn't think of
any. I've seen plenty of hilarious monster "bloopers" in which they
manage to kill themselves indirectly, but not like this.



